3. What is ported into this module
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Nothing is a verbatim Swift copy. The Swift tree is not vendored. Behaviour,
wire formats, numbers, byte tables and the bundled certificate are ported into
Kotlin. Each ported file names its source and pin in its own header.

Paths below are relative to src/<source set>/kotlin/app/aaps/plugins/libre3/.

3a. From LibreCRKit @ a86b92f (Swift paths as the file headers name them)

  crypto/Libre3LibAes.kt                  <- Crypto/LibAES.swift
  crypto/Libre3LibAesTables.kt            <- the LibAES table banks (3c)
  crypto/Libre3Phase5KeySchedule.kt       <- Crypto/Phase5KeySchedule.swift
  crypto/Libre3AesCcm.kt                  <- Crypto/AESCCM.swift
  crypto/Libre3DataPlaneCrypto.kt         <- DataPlane/DataPlaneCrypto.swift
  crypto/Libre3EphemeralKeys.kt           <- Pairing/SessionKey (first pair ephemeral)
  crypto/Libre3FirstPairPhase5Source.kt   <- Pairing/SessionKey
  crypto/Libre3PairingMessages.kt         <- Pairing/ChallengeMessage.swift,
                                             Pairing/Phase6Response.swift
  crypto/Libre3PhoneCert.kt               <- Pairing/PhoneCert.swift, including
                                             FirstPairStaticScalarWindow (3c)
  crypto/Libre3SensorCert.kt              <- Pairing/SensorCert.swift (the sensor
                                             maker's public signing keys)
  crypto/Libre3RuntimeTables.kt           <- the RuntimeTables folder (3c)
  crypto/firstpair/*.kt (25 files)        <- Crypto/FirstPairSourceSlice.swift
                                             (Libre3FirstPairVm.kt from its private
                                             vm... and step... helpers;
                                             Libre3FirstPairP256.kt has no header
