    libaes_keyexp_tables_275bbb.bin, libaes_round1_tables_278dc2.bin,
    libaes_round2_9_tables_279dc4.bin — the table banks of the Phase 5 wire
      block primitive.
    phase5_keysched_region_274000.bin — the static region the Phase 5 key
      schedule reads.
    sbox_19bit_lib_986819.bin (524,288 bytes) and
    child23_ttable_b_ext_976ea8_100000.bin (1,048,576 bytes) — the two large
      lookup tables that every step of the first pairing scheme reads.
    firstpair_633fa8_null_nibble_303a14.bin,
    firstpair_633fa8_null_tables_2fd1f1.bin,
    firstpair_633fa8_tail_fold_tables_2fe798.bin,
    firstpair_633fa8_tail_u32_low_tables_112528.bin,
    firstpair_6388f0_caller_loop_interleaved_2cdfa9.bin,
    firstpair_6388f0_lane_tables_302678.bin,
    firstpair_6388f0_low_loop_statics_2fe600.bin,
    firstpair_6388f0_low_seed_statics_2f4d28.bin,
    firstpair_6388f0_selector_add_119788.bin,
    firstpair_6388f0_selector_mul_116968.bin,
    firstpair_6388f0_shared_context_2cdae1.bin,
    firstpair_63c278_fold_tables_2feb18.bin,
    firstpair_63c278_u32_tables_112588.bin,
    firstpair_679f48_seed_tables_37075e.bin,
    firstpair_df80_round_tables_37120e.bin,
    firstpair_final_len_tables_372102.bin,
    firstpair_finalizer_tables_370e30.bin,
    firstpair_process2_public_tables_3038c0.bin,
    firstpair_reducer67ea28_nibble_373cf4.bin — the tables of the first
      pairing scheme.
    firstpair_prog_638840_2f5046.bin, firstpair_prog_64e2b8_3041b4.bin,
    firstpair_prog_67076c_35d3ef.bin, firstpair_prog_67cc18_369862.bin — the
      four small programs that the first pairing machines walk.

  Fixed values in the source code:
    crypto/Libre3PhoneCert.kt Libre3FirstPairStaticScalarWindow — a 32-byte
      scalar. Its header, ported from the upstream, calls it "the row 59 static
      scalar window of the sensor maker's certificate private index 1".
    crypto/Libre3SensorCert.kt KNOWN_SIGNING_KEYS — the sensor maker's public
      signing keys, used to check the sensor's certificate.

What this material is, in the words of the ported code itself:
  * crypto/firstpair/Libre3FirstPairConstants.kt: "The names are addresses and
    offsets inside the sensor maker's own library." The hex numbers in the
    file and table names above are such addresses.
  * crypto/firstpair/Libre3FirstPairVm.kt: "Each machine walks a short program
    taken out of a shipped table".
  * crypto/Libre3LibAes.kt: ported from LibAES.swift, "which is itself a clean
    room port of the sensor maker's own routine. It looks like AES but it is
    not: every step is driven by fixed tables that ship with the app".
  * crypto/Libre3Phase5KeySchedule.kt: "itself a clean room port of the sensor
    maker's own routine".
  * Upstream stated that these tables were produced by clean-room research on
    the sensor maker's own library and that they are fixed across users and
    installs.

So the tables, the phone certificate, the static scalar and the first pairing
code reproduce the behaviour of the sensor maker's (Abbott's) own library. See
section 5.

